sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant KServe as KServe ServingRuntime<br/>(Pod Manager)
    participant Istio as Istio Gateway<br/>(mTLS / Auth)
    participant API as vLLM API Server<br/>8000/TCP HTTP
    participant Engine as vLLM Engine<br/>(Inference Pipeline)
    participant Plugin as vllm_gaudi Plugin<br/>(HPU Backend)
    participant HPU as Intel Gaudi HPU<br/>(SynapseAI 1.23.0)
    participant Storage as Model Storage<br/>(Volume Mount)

    Note over KServe,API: Startup / Model Loading
    KServe->>API: Start container<br/>(UID 2000, non-root)
    API->>Engine: Initialize vLLM engine<br/>VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=hpu
    Engine->>Plugin: Register HPU device backend
    Plugin->>HPU: Initialize SynapseAI runtime<br/>PyTorch 2.9.0 HPU
    Engine->>Storage: Load model weights<br/>(configured storage path)
    Storage-->>Engine: Model artifacts
    Engine->>HPU: Transfer model to HPU memory
    HPU-->>Engine: Model ready

    Note over Client,HPU: Inference Request Flow
    Client->>Istio: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>Auth: Platform-managed
    Istio->>API: Forward request<br/>(mTLS if configured)
    API->>Engine: Enqueue inference request
    Engine->>Plugin: Execute forward pass
    Plugin->>HPU: Tensor operations<br/>(SynapseAI acceleration)
    HPU-->>Plugin: Computation result
    Plugin-->>Engine: Generated tokens
    Engine-->>API: Inference response
    API-->>Istio: JSON response
    Istio-->>Client: OpenAI-compatible response

    Note over Client,HPU: Build-time Dependency Flow
    Note right of Engine: Konflux build clones<br/>vllm-project/vllm@v0.16.0<br/>installs with VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=empty<br/>then installs vllm_gaudi<br/>with VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=hpu
